// Game: Postretro
// Format: Valve
// glossy-reflections-showcase dev map. One sealed room, interior x 0 to 480,
// y 0 to 480, z 0 to 192, walls 32 thick, built so glossy floor reflections
// read at a glance. The floor is two coplanar zones under one probe: the west
// two thirds, x 0 to 320, metal_mirror_tinted, sharp and tinted so it
// reflects strongly head-on; the east third, x 320 to 480,
// metal_satin_tinted, the same tint at a rougher sharpness. Twin
// signal-stripes columns and twin glowing pillars stand one on each zone, at
// the same distance from the south wall, so sharp and rough compare in one
// frame. Also on the sharp floor: a monument with a hazard-striped column
// near, and a parked kinematic block with hazard panels in the west. Light:
// a white light_area band across the north wall, a vertical light_area strip
// on the east wall, a magenta and a cyan point light and a white fill. The north
// wall is the glossy cyan and copper tile and reflects too; the east wall is
// hazard stripes; the west and south walls and the ceiling are matte metal
// panel. A reflection_volume over the room makes one probe for the floor and
// one for the north wall.
// Glossy placement runs only under prl-build --glossy-reflections.
// See glossy-reflections-showcase.README.md.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes, and never leave a blank
// line inside an entity block.
